# The build context is the whole repository (project references under src/ need to be in it), so what is excluded
# here is the difference between a fast build and shipping every local build output to the daemon.

# Build outputs — the big one. Without this the context carries the staged wasm bundle (~5 MB) and every bin/obj in
# the tree, none of which the image uses: the build stage compiles from source.
**/bin/
**/obj/
artifacts/
publish/

# Probe and client publish output, for the same reason. The reference host is Mode 2 and serves no browser client.
probe/*/bin/
clients/web/bin/
src/CupriNet.Nodestar.Client.CupriFace/client/

# Local run state. .run/ holds data directories from VS Code launches — each one contains a node identity and a
# site Signet, which have no business inside an image.
.run/
data/

.git/
.github/
.vscode/

# Documentation and tests: not needed to build the host, and they are the bulk of the file count.
design/
tests/
samples/
**/*.md

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
